 "intro": {
  "title": "THE HIVE YARDS, THE DARK",
  "lines": [
   "A lantern, sleepers and a creature that rings: the noise tell and the lamp that holds sound back.",
   "Every weapon. Nothing runs out. You cannot die. L lights the lantern. F8 slows the game."
  ]
 },
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "hub",
   "at": [70, 40],
   "radius": 8,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "THE HIVE YARDS, THE DARK (dev): west the sleepers' yard (the noise tell), east the lamp yard (the lamp holds sound back). L lights the lantern. Nothing can kill you here."
  },
  {
   "id": "exit",
   "at": [70, 48],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "THE EXIT is south of here: it goes back to the title."
  },
  {
   "id": "sy",
   "at": [41, 40],
   "radius": 6,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "THE SLEEPERS' YARD. Ten sleep among the columns. The HUD says QUIET or LOUD for the gun in hand and how far a shot carries (Tab: the ring). The arc, the fork and a blow are quiet."
  },
  {
   "id": "sy2",
   "at": [24, 40],
   "radius": 8,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "Judge: is the tell useful (do you change weapon for it)? Is 6 m dark / 24 m lit a fair way to be seen? Is the quiet kill a real option? (Pause, Restart puts them back to sleep.)"
  },
  {
   "id": "sy3",
   "at": [8, 40],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The far wall. The sleepers still asleep are the ones you passed quietly."
  },
  {
   "id": "ly",
   "at": [99, 40],
   "radius": 7,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "THE LAMP YARD. The Sub-Cantor cannot be killed; its ring reaches 22 m. L lights the lantern: a ring is cut to 0.6. West-wall levers: the plain lantern, or Ines's own (0.4)."
  },
  {
   "id": "ly2",
   "at": [112, 48],
   "radius": 8,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "Judge: is the lamp a real trade (it is the only way to take less, but creatures that follow light see you from 24 m) or a fiddly one? Are cover and the ledge better answers?"
  }
 ],
